mke2fs's defaults for ext4 are the configuration the LikeOS root image is
built with (top-level Makefile: EXT4_MKFS_FEATURES and the mkfs.ext4 call)
and the LikeOS ext4 driver is verified against: has_journal, extent,
huge_file, flex_bg, metadata_csum, dir_nlink, extra_isize on top of the base
features, 4 KiB blocks for every size class.  Dropped from the upstream
default: 64bit (32-byte group descriptors, as in the image),
metadata_csum_seed and orphan_file (not in the image), and the 1 KiB block
size of the "small" and "floppy" classes (the image is always 4 KiB).
auto_64-bit_support turns 64bit back on only for a device whose block count
does not fit in 32 bits (16 TiB at 4 KiB blocks), where mke2fs would
otherwise refuse; the driver implements 64bit.  The same text is mke2fs's
built-in profile and the installed /etc/mke2fs.conf.

